/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
/dist

# THE APPRENTICE's working files.
#
# A proof is `(seed, mode, difficulty, [verb])` and it is as long as the run it
# proves: a fifty-three-rung run is forty-five thousand presses even after the
# trial seats cancel out, which is half a megabyte of keys. The spec's "a few
# KB each" was written when nothing had played a run.
#
# So **one** proof is committed - the deepest, as the mission's evidence - and
# the rest are made on demand by `--bin proof`. They are reproducible from
# their own headers, which is what makes them not-source.
/crates/*/target
/artifacts
/runs
*.mpk
*.safetensors
analysis/proofs/*.proof
!analysis/proofs/C434E4A68C5906EE-grinder-medium.proof

# Trained checkpoints land beside whatever ran the trainer. The two that a
# measurement in `analysis/` refers to are kept in `analysis/nets/`; the rest
# are output, not source.
runs/
q8/
